# what a bell does of itself and what it wants (docs/OVERHAUL.md section 3; SEEDING section 4, the
# seventh rain), carried to every bell by under and owned by the kind's owner: it rings at its seventh
# rain, notes its planter when it rings, and wants a first rain, a rain from a second hand, and
# tending once it has gone quiet. Tending (world/bodies/bell.obend quietAfter): a bell answers while
# tended within 1440 clock minutes, and untended past it takes tend alone (tests/test_tending.py
# compares the two). A rain is a line whose verb is rain (a hand's, the weather's); a grown verb's
# gesture is no rain
of: record
form: <<END
colour: amber | violet | silver
seed: text 1..80
END
voice: small and brass, tuned rather than struck; it waits for rain, and scatters light when it rings
about: rings at its seventh rain; goes quiet untended a day
text: <<END
law alive "answers while tended within 1440 minutes": request.method == "tend" or request.kind == rule or request.clock <= old.tended + 1440
rule seven "rings at its seventh rain": count(new.lines where verb == "rain") >= 7 and count(old.lines where verb == "rain") <= 6 then delvetalk {request.object} ring
rule rang "notes its planter when it rings": "rung" in new.marks.name and not "rung" in old.marks.name then delvetalk {new.maker} note / text: {request.object} rang
want rain "a bell nobody has rained on": count(new.lines where verb == "rain") == 0 asks delvetalk {request.object} rain
want second "a bell only its planter has rained on": count(new.lines where verb == "rain") >= 1 and count(new.lines where verb == "rain" and author == new.maker) >= count(new.lines where verb == "rain") asks delvetalk {request.object} rain
want tend "a bell gone quiet, untended a day": request.clock >= new.tended + 1441 asks delvetalk {request.object} tend
END
body: bell
